            {
                "comment": "Not many tests but you do need to study for them since they are usually harder than the things studied in class. Most of the class is graded on essays that you write. Wouldn't recommend skipping class since you will miss a lot of what he covers and it hurts your participation.  ",
                "difficulty_rating": 3,
                "quality_rating": 4
            },
            {
                "comment": "Santiago is a great TA! I loved going to his class! He kept things interesting! He's a fair and fun teacher. Don't let him intimidate you on the first day like he tries to! He's actually super friendly! I highly recommend him!",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Santiago is a great TA! He's a cool guy, very personable, and a fair grader. He's pretty big on participation and literature, but he is also very willing to help you get a good grade in the class.",
                "difficulty_rating": 2,
                "quality_rating": 5
            },
            {
                "comment": "Santiago is an extremely tough professor. He is always willing to help and the work you do with him pays off in the end on the final. Just make sure you go to class and GO TO OFFICE HOURS. Also be sure to speak up in class because he is big on participation, especially during the last unit.",
                "difficulty_rating": 5,
                "quality_rating": 3
